<div class="card" id="linux">
<h2>Linux: First Lesson</h2>
<p><b>pwd</b> displays your current directory.</p>
<p><b>ls</b> lists files and folders.</p>
<p><b>whoami</b> displays your current username.</p>
</div>

<div class="card" id="network">
<h2>Networking: First Lesson</h2>
<p>127.0.0.1 is the loopback address.</p>
<p>Port 8000 is the port used by our local lab.</p>
<p>HTTP is a protocol used to transfer web content.</p>
</div>

<div class="card" id="python">
<h2>Python: First Lesson</h2>
<p>Python lets us create our own security utilities.</p>
<pre>print("NIGHTHAWK ONLINE")</pre>
</div>

<div class="card" id="web">
<h2>Web Security: First Lesson</h2>
<p>Learn HTTP requests, responses, headers and web vulnerabilities.</p>
</div>

<div class="card" id="passwords">
<h2>Password Security: First Lesson</h2>
<p>Learn secure hashing, salts and password storage.</p>
</div>

